      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Yeah, I think it's doing something weird because my eye bone at 0 doesn't look straight forward, it looks somewhat down. It looks like it's transforming the eyes but still reporting the rotation as 0.\n\nThe current Unity settings (in which the bones are transformed 11 degrees to look \"forward\", with the same transform set in the Eye Look to make it look forward).  \n\nThe last picture is with my VRCFT tracking turned on with no data input, so it's what the raycasts do when my avatar is looking forward as set in Unity.",
