  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The native eye tracking seems to use the bone's native rotation point as zero, rather than the center of \"look forward\" set in descriptor\n\nIt seems to happen when the eye bone isn't at 0 rotation on the skeleton. Transforming it to -11 and then using the Descriptor to have Look Forward at -11 seems to double it up, so it looks upward when it should be casting forward.\n\nSetting the eyelook forward at 0 seems to fix this for now, it looks ahead despite the preview in the Descriptor looking down. I'll try to report more on this once I figure out more.",
